				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-0c254ff elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="0c254ff" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<h2><strong>Airports We’ve Worked With</strong></h2><p>We’ve built airports water feature projects for several locations, including McAllen International Airport in Texas and the Central Illinois Regional Airport. Each had its own goals and space, but both wanted to make travelers feel more at ease while waiting.</p><p>At McAllen, the water feature adds movement to a seating area without needing constant maintenance. In Central Illinois, we built a feature that fits the architecture and adds a quiet touch to the waiting zone.</p><p>These airports wanted something that worked well and didn’t take up too much time for staff to manage. That’s what we delivered. If your team needs help figuring out how a water feature might fit into your space, we’ll walk you through ideas and show examples that fit your layout.</p><p> </p>								</div>
